{
    "attributes": {
        "action": "Legislate to restrict Ofgem\u2019s ability to mandate compensation for customer loss",
        "additional_details": "In our view this works as a switching penalty, weakens competition and could make cheaper deals cost more. We think that by making suppliers that win customers compensate those that lose them, it weakens price competition, risks raising the cost of the cheapest deals, and shields suppliers from commercial risks they are paid to manage. We also believe that it\u2019s in conflict to the government\u2019s removal of the 5% VAT rate on domestic electricity bills to reduce consumers\u2019 bills.",
        "background": "Legislate to restrict Ofgem\u2019s ability to require companies to compensate competitors for lost customers. With its Market Stabilisation Charge Ofgem proposes that a supplier winning a customer must pay the customer's old supplier when wholesale prices fall sharply. ",
